A1_infl_breadth_mom — inflation-proxy breadth momentum (A1 r6, SAVED 2026-08-30)
Window 2008-01-03..2026-07-01, n=4825.

ECONOMIC RATIONALE: The xau/slv/wti/copper basket is a broad real-asset complex; its
trend breadth is a slow inflation-regime indicator. When a majority of hard-asset
markets are in uptrends, the equal-weight complex earns an inflation-risk-premium and
momentum drift that equities/bonds do not pay (book is +35.4% in 2021 and +18.4% in
2022 — the stagflation years when bond/equity books bled — and +2.1% in 2008). Majority
breadth (>1/2 of legs up) is far more robust than any single-asset trend or pair ratio
(xau/copper ratio trend standalone SR 0.65 with a -44% year; copper alone is too thin;
the 3-leg charter trio without silver scores only 0.67).

CONSTRUCTION: signal_t = 1{ #{126d return > 0} over {xau,slv,wti,copper} > 0.5 };
ret = equal-weight basket daily return; funding rf + lev*(ret - rf) (honest, no phantom
carry); T+1 execution (lev at t earns t+1 excess); cost 6bps x |dlev| one-side, charged t+1;
vol-target 10% ann via expanding(min 60d) std SHIFT(1) (trailing-only), leverage cap 2.
Copper is FRED monthly, publication-lagged to next month start (no-lag variant SR 1.23
is VOID — lookahead class; disclosed in FINDINGS r3/r6).

PARAMS: L=126d, thr=0.5, vt=10%, cap=2.0, members={xau,slv,wti,cop}, rf=tbill3m/252.
Repro: campaign/scripts/a1_inflation_breadth.py (seed 20260828 for scramble).

